---
name: sign_in_code
to: '{{ data.to }}'
from: >
  {%- include 'emails/autoresponder_from' -%}
reply_to: >
  {%- include 'emails/autoresponder_reply_to' -%}
subject: Your sign-in code
metadata: {
  email_name: 'Sign-In Code'
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  Sent by app/views/pages/account/sign_in_code_request_submit.liquid through
  app/graphql/account/sign_in/send_sign_in_code.graphql. data: { to, code, minutes }.
  The code is in the body only, never the subject, so it does not show in notification previews.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333; text-align: center; padding: 24px;">
  <p style="font-size: 24px;"><strong>Your sign-in code</strong></p>
  <p>Enter this code on the sign-in page:</p>
  <p style="font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 8px;"><strong>{{ data.code | escape }}</strong></p>
  <p>It works once, for {{ data.minutes | escape }} minutes. Asking for a new code stops this one working.</p>
  <p>If you did not ask for a code, ignore this email. Nobody can sign in with it unless they can read your email.</p>
</div>
